Feature: Backup and Vacuum Operations for customer_360_raw Table

  The system must efficiently back up the purgo_databricks.purgo_playground.customer_360_raw table as compressed parquet files partitioned by state in the specified Databricks volume, and perform a vacuum operation to retain only records from the last 30 days. All operations must be logged in purgo_playground.customer_360_raw_backup_log.

  Background:
    Given the source table is purgo_databricks.purgo_playground.customer_360_raw
    And the backup volume path is /Volumes/customer_360_raw_backup
    And the backup parquet files must be compressed using snappy codec
    And the backup must include all columns from the source table
    And the backup must be a full backup (all records)
    And the vacuum operation must retain only records where creation_date >= current_date - 30 days
    And the backup and vacuum operations must be logged in purgo_playground.customer_360_raw_backup_log with fields: timestamp, status, operation_type, record_count, error_message
    And the backup and vacuum operations are triggered manually

  Scenario: Successful backup of customer_360_raw table to compressed parquet files partitioned by state
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains 10000 records with valid data
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then all 10000 records are written as parquet files to /Volumes/customer_360_raw_backup
    And the parquet files are compressed using snappy codec
    And the files are partitioned by the "state" column
    And the backup operation status is logged as "SUCCESS" in customer_360_raw_backup_log with operation_type "BACKUP" and record_count 10000
    And no error_message is recorded

  Scenario: Successful vacuum of customer_360_raw table retaining only last 30 days of records
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains records with creation_date ranging from 2023-01-01 to current_date
    When the vacuum operation is triggered
    Then only records with creation_date >= current_date - 30 days remain in the table
    And all records older than 30 days are permanently removed
    And the vacuum operation status is logged as "SUCCESS" in customer_360_raw_backup_log with operation_type "VACUUM" and record_count equal to the number of records retained
    And no error_message is recorded

  Scenario Outline: Backup operation fails due to invalid volume path
    Given the backup volume path is "<invalid_path>"
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then no parquet files are written
    And the backup operation status is logged as "FAILURE" in customer_360_raw_backup_log with operation_type "BACKUP" and record_count 0
    And the error_message contains "Invalid volume path: <invalid_path>"

    Examples:
      | invalid_path                  |
      | /Volumes/nonexistent_backup   |
      | /Volumes/customer_360_invalid |

  Scenario: Backup operation fails due to insufficient storage space
    Given the backup volume path is /Volumes/customer_360_raw_backup
    And the volume has less than 1GB free space
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then no parquet files are written
    And the backup operation status is logged as "FAILURE" in customer_360_raw_backup_log with operation_type "BACKUP" and record_count 0
    And the error_message contains "Insufficient storage space"

  Scenario: Vacuum operation fails due to table lock
    Given the customer_360_raw table is locked by another process
    When the vacuum operation is triggered
    Then no records are removed
    And the vacuum operation status is logged as "FAILURE" in customer_360_raw_backup_log with operation_type "VACUUM" and record_count 0
    And the error_message contains "Table is locked"

  Scenario: Backup operation fails due to missing source table
    Given the customer_360_raw table does not exist
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then no parquet files are written
    And the backup operation status is logged as "FAILURE" in customer_360_raw_backup_log with operation_type "BACKUP" and record_count 0
    And the error_message contains "Source table not found"

  Scenario: Vacuum operation fails due to missing source table
    Given the customer_360_raw table does not exist
    When the vacuum operation is triggered
    Then no records are removed
    And the vacuum operation status is logged as "FAILURE" in customer_360_raw_backup_log with operation_type "VACUUM" and record_count 0
    And the error_message contains "Source table not found"

  Scenario Outline: Backup operation fails due to write permission error
    Given the backup volume path is "<restricted_path>"
    And the user does not have write permission to the volume
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then no parquet files are written
    And the backup operation status is logged as "FAILURE" in customer_360_raw_backup_log with operation_type "BACKUP" and record_count 0
    And the error_message contains "Permission denied: <restricted_path>"

    Examples:
      | restricted_path                |
      | /Volumes/customer_360_raw_backup |
      | /Volumes/protected_backup        |

  Scenario: Backup operation includes all columns and preserves data types
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains columns: id (bigint), name (string), email (string), phone (string), company (string), job_title (string), address (string), city (string), state (string), country (string), industry (string), account_manager (string), creation_date (date), last_interaction_date (date), purchase_history (string), notes (string), zip (string)
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then the parquet files contain all columns with matching data types as in the source table

  Scenario: Backup operation overwrites previous backup files for the same partition
    Given the backup volume path is /Volumes/customer_360_raw_backup
    And parquet files for state="CA" already exist from a previous backup
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then the new parquet files for state="CA" overwrite the previous files

  Scenario: Logging of backup and vacuum operations
    Given a backup or vacuum operation is triggered
    When the operation completes (success or failure)
    Then a log entry is created in customer_360_raw_backup_log with the following fields:
      | timestamp         | ISO 8601 format, e.g., "2024-07-30T12:34:56Z" |
      | status            | "SUCCESS" or "FAILURE"                        |
      | operation_type    | "BACKUP" or "VACUUM"                          |
      | record_count      | Number of records processed                   |
      | error_message     | Error details if status is "FAILURE", else null |

  Scenario: Data validation - backup file row count matches source table
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains 5000 records
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then the total number of rows in the backup parquet files is 5000

  Scenario: Data validation - partitioning by state
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains records with state values: "CA", "NY", "TX"
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then the backup parquet files are partitioned into directories: /Volumes/customer_360_raw_backup/state=CA, /Volumes/customer_360_raw_backup/state=NY, /Volumes/customer_360_raw_backup/state=TX

  Scenario: Data validation - parquet file compression
    Given the backup operation is triggered
    Then all output parquet files are compressed using snappy codec

  Scenario: Data validation - vacuum operation removes only records older than 30 days
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains records with creation_date values both older and newer than current_date - 30 days
    When the vacuum operation is triggered
    Then only records with creation_date < current_date - 30 days are removed
    And records with creation_date >= current_date - 30 days remain

  Scenario: Data validation - vacuum operation does not remove recent records
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains only records with creation_date >= current_date - 30 days
    When the vacuum operation is triggered
    Then no records are removed
    And the vacuum operation status is logged as "SUCCESS" with record_count equal to the total number of records

  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation does not mask or exclude any columns
    Given the backup operation is triggered
    Then all columns from the source table are present in the backup parquet files
    And no columns are masked or excluded

  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation preserves null values
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains records with null values in some columns
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then the corresponding fields in the backup parquet files are also null

  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation preserves data quality
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains records with special characters, unicode, and long text in string columns
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then the backup parquet files preserve all data without truncation or corruption

  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation preserves date formats
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains creation_date and last_interaction_date columns with valid date values
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then the date values in the backup parquet files match the source table

  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation handles empty source table
    Given the customer_360_raw table is empty
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then no parquet files are written
    And the backup operation status is logged as "SUCCESS" with record_count 0

  Scenario: Data validation - vacuum operation handles empty source table
    Given the customer_360_raw table is empty
    When the vacuum operation is triggered
    Then no records are removed
    And the vacuum operation status is logged as "SUCCESS" with record_count 0

  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation handles duplicate records
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains duplicate records
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then all records, including duplicates, are written to the backup parquet files

  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation handles large datasets
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains 10,000,000 records
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then all 10,000,000 records are written as parquet files to /Volumes/customer_360_raw_backup
    And the operation completes without data loss

  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation handles all supported state values
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains records with all valid US state codes
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then the backup parquet files are partitioned by each state code present in the data

  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation handles special characters in state values
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains records with state values containing spaces or special characters
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then the backup parquet files are partitioned using the exact state values, preserving special characters

  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation handles null state values
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains records with null in the state column
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then the backup parquet files include a partition for state=null

  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation handles non-ASCII characters in string columns
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains records with non-ASCII characters in name, address, or notes columns
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then the backup parquet files preserve all non-ASCII characters

  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation handles long text fields
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains records with notes or purchase_history fields longer than 1000 characters
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then the backup parquet files preserve the full text without truncation

  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation handles all nullable columns
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains null values in any nullable column
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then the backup parquet files preserve nulls in the corresponding columns

  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation preserves record order (if required)
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains records in a specific order
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then the backup parquet files do not guarantee order unless explicitly sorted

  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation does not modify source table
    Given the backup operation is triggered
    Then the customer_360_raw table remains unchanged

  Scenario: Data validation - vacuum operation does not affect backup files
    Given the vacuum operation is triggered
    Then the backup parquet files in /Volumes/customer_360_raw_backup remain unchanged

  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation does not update customer_360_raw_backup table
    Given the backup operation is triggered
    Then the customer_360_raw_backup table is not modified

  Scenario: Data validation - backup and vacuum operations are idempotent
    Given the backup and vacuum operations are triggered multiple times with no data changes
    When the operations are triggered again
    Then the results and log entries are consistent with previous runs

  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation handles concurrent execution
    Given two backup operations are triggered simultaneously
    When both operations run
    Then only one set of backup files is written per partition
    And both operations are logged in customer_360_raw_backup_log

  Scenario: Data validation - vacuum operation handles concurrent execution
    Given two vacuum operations are triggered simultaneously
    When both operations run
    Then only one vacuum operation completes successfully
    And both operations are logged in customer_360_raw_backup_log

  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation handles schema evolution (new columns)
    Given the customer_360_raw table schema is updated with a new column "customer_segment" (string)
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then the backup parquet files include the new column with correct data type

  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation handles schema evolution (dropped columns)
    Given the customer_360_raw table schema has a column "legacy_id" (bigint) that is dropped
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then the backup parquet files do not include the dropped column

  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation handles schema evolution (column type change)
    Given the customer_360_raw table column "zip" changes from string to integer
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then the backup parquet files store "zip" as integer

  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation handles empty partitions
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains no records for state="NV"
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then no partition directory is created for state="NV"

  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation handles case sensitivity in state values
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains records with state values "ca", "CA", "Ca"
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then partition directories are created for each distinct state value as present in the data

  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation handles whitespace in state values
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains records with state values " CA ", "CA"
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then partition directories are created for each distinct state value as present in the data, including whitespace

  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation handles special characters in file paths
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains state values with special characters (e.g., "N/A", "Unknown-State")
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then partition directories are created using the exact state values, encoding special characters as required by the file system

  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation handles large number of partitions
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains records with 1000 unique state values
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then 1000 partition directories are created in /Volumes/customer_360_raw_backup

  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation handles records with missing state values
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains records with null or empty string in the state column
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then a partition directory is created for state=null and/or state=""

  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation handles records with future creation_date
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains records with creation_date > current_date
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then all records are backed up regardless of creation_date

  Scenario: Data validation - vacuum operation does not remove records with future creation_date
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains records with creation_date > current_date
    When the vacuum operation is triggered
    Then records with creation_date > current_date are retained

  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation handles records with invalid email or phone formats
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains records with invalid email or phone formats
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then all records are backed up without validation or modification of email or phone formats

  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation handles records with special unicode characters
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains records with special unicode characters in any string column
    When the backup operation is triggered
