  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation handles records with special characters in file names
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains state values with characters not allowed in file names (e.g., "/", "\", ":", "*", "?", "\"", "<", ">", "|")
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then partition directories are created with sanitized or encoded state values as required by the file system

  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation handles records with leading/trailing whitespace in state values
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains records with state values " CA", "CA ", " CA "
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then partition directories are created for each distinct state value as present in the data, including whitespace

  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation handles records with mixed case state values
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains records with state values "ca", "CA", "Ca"
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then partition directories are created for each distinct state value as present in the data

  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation handles records with null values in all columns except id
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains records where all columns except id are null
    When the backup operation is triggered
    Then the backup parquet files preserve nulls in all columns except id

  Scenario: Data validation - backup operation handles records with duplicate ids
    Given the customer_360_raw table contains records with duplicate id values
    When the backup operation is triggered
